# Conclusion

The Strict profile behaves much closer to a protocol reviewer than a social-media evaluator.

The strongest predictor of acceptance is not technical quality alone, but explicit and direct relevance to GenLayer. 
Posts discussing Intelligent Contracts, GenVM, Optimistic Democracy, validators, Equivalence Principle, deployment metrics, 
or protocol-specific research consistently outperform otherwise strong but generic technical content.

Research remains the highest-performing category, but only when clearly tied to measurable GenLayer properties. 
Generic blockchain or AI research is frequently rejected despite respectable technical scores.

The most significant finding is the complete elimination of meme content. Even memes receiving strong relevance, tone, 
and engagement scores were rejected because the profile prioritizes substantive informational value over entertainment.

Overall, the Strict profile heavily rewards protocol-focused, educational, and research-driven 
content while aggressively filtering generic discussion, humor, promotion, and ecosystem-adjacent material.
